### High-Card — Auth endpoints
# 1. Run "Login as alice" / "Login as bob" below to receive a JWT.
# 2. Copy the token string from each response into the matching variable
#    below (`@adminToken` for alice, `@userToken` for bob).
# 3. Run the protected requests further down — they reference the variables.
# Tokens stay valid for `app.jwt.expiration-minutes` (default 60).

@host = http://localhost:8080
@adminToken = paste-alice-token-here
@userToken = paste-bob-token-here

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### POSITIVE — Login (POST /auth/login)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Login as alice (admin) — copy the response `token` into @adminToken above
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### Login as bob (user) — copy the response `token` into @userToken above
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "user123"
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### NEGATIVE — Login failures
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Wrong password — should return 200 + status.code 401
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### Unknown user — should return 200 + status.code 401
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ghost",
  "password": "whatever"
}

### Missing username — validation 400
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "admin123"
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Sample protected call — uses {{token}}
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Search users with valid token
POST {{host}}/user/v1/user
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "query": null,
  "offset": 0,
  "limit": 10,
  "order": "BY_LASTNAME"
}

### Search users without token — should return 200 + status.code 401
POST {{host}}/user/v1/user
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": null,
  "offset": 0,
  "limit": 10,
  "order": "BY_LASTNAME"
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Authorization (RBAC) — admin vs user
### Run alice's and bob's logins first to populate adminToken / userToken.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Add user with admin token (alice) — should succeed (200 + status.code 200)
PUT {{host}}/user/v1/user
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "firstName": "Authorized",
  "lastName": "Adminsson",
  "email": "auth.admin@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+39 3331112222"
}

### Add user with USER-only token (bob) — should return 200 + status.code 403
PUT {{host}}/user/v1/user
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "firstName": "Should",
  "lastName": "Fail",
  "email": "should.fail@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+39 3334445555"
}

### Search users with USER-only token (bob) — should succeed
POST {{host}}/user/v1/user
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "query": null,
  "offset": 0,
  "limit": 10,
  "order": "BY_LASTNAME"
}
